1. MOCK BACKEND SETUP
- Installed json-server devDependency (npm install --save-dev json-server@0.17.4)
- Created db.json in project root with courses, students, and enrollments endpoints

2. HTTPCLIENT REFACTORING (CourseService)
- Imported HttpClientModule in AppModule
- Refactored CourseService to execute HTTP requests to http://localhost:3000/courses:
  * getCourses(): GET Observable<Course[]>
  * getCourseById(id): GET Observable<Course>
  * createCourse(course): POST Observable<Course>
  * updateCourse(course): PUT Observable<Course>
  * deleteCourse(id): DELETE Observable<void>

3. RXJS OPERATORS & ERROR HANDLING
- retry(2): Automatically retries failed HTTP requests twice
- map: Filters and transforms API course data streams
- tap: Executes side-effect logging without mutating stream data
  * Comment added explaining why tap is preferred over map for logging
- catchError: Handles client and server errors gracefully with user-friendly throwError
- switchMap: Demonstrated in getCourseStudents(courseId$)
  * Comment added explaining how switchMap cancels previous inner Observables to prevent race conditions

4. HTTP INTERCEPTORS (Registered via HTTP_INTERCEPTORS multi-provider)
- AuthInterceptor (src/app/interceptors/auth.interceptor.ts):
  * Clones HttpRequest and adds 'Authorization: Bearer mocktoken-12345' header
- ErrorHandlerInterceptor (src/app/interceptors/error-handler.interceptor.ts):
  * Catches HTTP errors globally (status 401 redirect, status 500 alert)
- LoadingInterceptor (src/app/interceptors/loading.interceptor.ts):
  * Toggles LoadingService BehaviorSubject (show on request start, hide in finalize)

